t to Finish

I had an outstanding experience working with Morelli Medical, and especiall=
y with Nuke Paz, who handled my purchase of the OxyRevo Forward 90 (1.5 ATA=
) hyperbaric oxygen chamber.

From the very beginning, Nuke stood out as someone who was focused on helpi=
ng me make the right decision, not just making a sale. He took the time to =
answer my questions thoughtfully, helped me understand which options were g=
enuinely useful for my situation, and=E2=80=94just as importantly=E2=80=94p=
ointed out what I didn=E2=80=99t need. At no point did I feel like I was de=
aling with a high-pressure salesperson chasing a commission. The integrity =
and transparency made it easy to trust the process.

They also gave me a very fair and competitive deal, and the follow-through =
was excellent. I received frequent updates throughout the entire process=E2=
=80=94from production overseas to shipping logistics to final delivery at m=
y door. Communication didn=E2=80=99t stop once the chamber arrived either. =
Nuke and the team continued to be available to help with setup, operation q=
uestions, and ongoing support, which made a big difference.

I=E2=80=99m extremely happy with the OxyRevo 1.5 ATA chamber itself, and ju=
st as happy with the company behind it. This is how medical-adjacent equipm=
ent should be sold: knowledgeable, ethical, responsive, and supportive.

I would absolutely purchase from Morelli Medical again and recommend them w=
ithout hesitation.

=E2=80=94 John</div></div><div class=3D"go1481296246 reputon-single-review"=
